## Invariants

- Binding hash is `sha256.Sum256` of the raw artifact slice, lowercase hex, identical to `artifactstore.hashBytes`. No trimming, normalization or prompt-envelope bytes participate. A trailing-newline difference is a mismatch.
- Every stage output already carries a valid SHA-256 (`validateArtifactRef` at `internal/runmanifest/manifest.go:797`), so there is no digestless output branch. The gate never skips binding.
- The mismatch check happens after `latestStageForRole` and before tier resolution, `nextPhaseRound`, prompt build, `MkdirAll(ScratchDir)`, checks and seats. Nothing is written on mismatch.
- The bytes hashed are the same `req.Artifact` slice passed to `buildGatePrompt`. No second read.
- Manifest validation keeps all existing identifier and digest-format checks. Gate ordering relative to stages is unchanged: all stages are indexed before any gate is validated, so no temporal or forward-reference policy is introduced.
- Stage names are never rewritten. No `.rN` auto-naming, no occurrence index, no sequence field, no schema version bump, no migration. Repeated identical digests under the same name remain ambiguous for producer metadata; that is a pre-existing schema limit and is out of scope.
- The generic validator stays output/log/input aware. Only the supervised gate binds to output specifically.

## Design

### 1. `internal/liverun/gate_once.go`

After resolving `reviewed`:

```go
supplied := hex.EncodeToString(sha256sum(req.Artifact))
if supplied != reviewed.Output.Artifact {
    return GateOutcome{}, fmt.Errorf("%w: run %s stage %q output role %q is %s but the supplied artifact is %s; recapture it first (etude capture %s --run %s --expect append --output %s=<artifact-path>, where <artifact-path> is the file given to gate --artifact) then rerun this gate",
        ErrArtifactMismatch, req.RunID, reviewed.Name, req.Stage.Produces, reviewed.Output.Artifact, supplied, reviewed.Name, req.RunID, req.Stage.Produces)
}
```

Add `var ErrArtifactMismatch = errors.New("gate artifact does not match captured output")` next to `ErrNoReviewableStage`. Imports `crypto/sha256` and `encoding/hex`. Nothing else in the function moves; the check sits at line 115, immediately after the `ErrNoReviewableStage` return. The recorded `ReviewedStages[0].Artifact` stays `reviewed.Output.Artifact`, which is now provably equal to the supplied digest.

The CLI in `internal/cli/gate.go` needs no new request field. `runGateCommand` already holds `cfg.artifactPath`; wrap `ErrArtifactMismatch` there only if the placeholder text is judged unhelpful. Default: leave the CLI untouched, the engine message is already actionable. Reviewer may request the CLI substitution; it is a two-line `errors.Is` wrap.

### 2. `internal/runmanifest/manifest.go`

Change the validation index at line 312 from `map[string]Stage` to `map[string][]Stage`, appending every occurrence. `validateGate` takes the new type. Reference resolution:

```go
occurrences, ok := stageIndex[ref.Stage]   // missing name: unchanged error
if ref.Artifact != "" {
    // format check unchanged
    found := false
    for _, s := range occurrences { if stageHasArtifact(s, ref.Artifact) { found = true; break } }
    if !found { return existing "not found on stage ... output or inputs" error }
}
```

Error text keeps the existing prefix so current tests and docs stay valid; append "(any stage named ...)" only if a reviewer asks. `stageHasArtifact` is unchanged.

### 3. Consumers checked, no change

- `internal/liverun/gate.go:498` `stageByReviewedRef` already matches name and output digest walking backwards. Unchanged.
- `internal/cli/run.go:410` prints refs verbatim. Unchanged.
- `internal/cli/capture.go` `capture-gate` serializes refs and relies on `Validate`. Gains the relaxed rule for free.
- `latestStageForRole` (engine.go:76) still picks the newest occurrence for a role, which is the intended recapture semantics: after a corrected capture the next gate reviews the newest bytes.

### 4. Tests

